id: pm-9x9drr
title: "pm package manage --fix-managed-state holds the extension state lock across every remote update lookup, so a raised update-check budget lengthens how long concurrent package actions wait"
description: "Raised by CodeRabbit on PR 1752 (outside-diff comment on src/sdk/extension.ts, the prepareExploreManageState path). With --fix-managed-state, dispatchExtensionAction wraps the whole manage handler in withExtensionInstallLock. That handler adopts unmanaged packages and then calls refreshManagedExtensionUpdates, so the lock stays held while every npm view and git ls-remote runs, four at a time. The refresh never persists its result, so it does not need the lock. Behaviour is unchanged at the default 10-second budget, but PM_EXTENSION_UPDATE_CHECK_TIMEOUT_MS (pm-5kfzjh) can raise each lookup to 120 seconds. A concurrent install, uninstall or adopt then waits longer for the lock and can fail with a lock conflict. Proposed: keep only the adoption read and write under the lock, and run the refresh and runtime probe after it is released."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 3
tags[4]: concurrency,extensions,locking,update-check
created_at: "2026-11-18T10:52:10.869Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-18T11:24:36.122Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "manage --fix-managed-state holds the extension state lock only for the adoption read and write; the remote update refresh and runtime probe run after the lock is released, with the same results and offline behaviour; a test proves a concurrent locked package action is not blocked by a slow lookup; manage without --fix-managed-state is unchanged"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
severity: low
expected_result: A slow or long-budget update lookup never holds the extension state lock
actual_result: "With --fix-managed-state the lock spans every remote update lookup, up to the configured budget per lookup"
component: extensions
